#. Tag: title
#: using-setup-editor-raw.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "RAW Decoding Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-editor-raw.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the early versions of &digikam; the Image Editor was just a viewer for "
"photographs, but it is rapidly developing into a very useful photo "
"manipulation tool. This dialog allows you to control how the Image Editor "
"will behave when opening RAW files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: using-setup-editor-raw.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fast and simple, as 8 bit image"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-editor-raw.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"RAW files will be decoded to 8-bit color depth with a BT.709 gamma curve and "
"a 99th-percentile white point. This mode is faster than 16-bit decoding. In "
"8-bit mode only the <guilabel>Auto Brightness</guilabel> setting will be "
"taken into account (dcraw limitation)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: using-setup-editor-raw.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use the default settings, in 16 bit"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-editor-raw.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, all RAW files will be decoded to 16-bit color depth using a "
"linear gamma curve and according to the settings in the <guilabel>RAW "
"Default Settings</guilabel> tab. To prevent dark image rendering in the "
"editor, it is recommended to use Color Management in this mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: using-setup-editor-raw.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "Always open the Raw Import Tool to customize settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-editor-raw.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this option checked the Raw Import Tool will open at the Right Side Bar "
"in the Image Editor so that you can set individual parameters for every "
"image you open."
msgstr ""

#~ msgid "Color Management"
#~ msgstr "Xestión de color"
